  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}-8{y}^{\u2032}+15y=0,\\,y(0)=2,\\,{y}^{\u2032}(0)=2.\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +15 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -5) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =3,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{3x}+B{e}^{5x}.\n$$\n\nNow we find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B=2.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{\u2032}(0)=2,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=3A{e}^{3x}+5B{e}^{5x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{\u2032}(0)=2$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n3A+5B=2.\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}A+B=2 \\\\ 3A+5B=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=4,B=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4{e}^{3x}-2{e}^{5x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
